   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## ltxv-guides.json\n\nKeyframe animation: our stills pinned at chosen frames\n\n**Does:** two stills + a prompt -> a clip that travels between the stills. **Chained `LTXVAddGuide` route\n(2026-11-23):** each guide node pins one still at its `frame_idx` on the 97-frame timeline - the indices are\n**editable widgets**, no offline guide-clip build. The latent stays empty (`EmptyLTXVLatentVideo`): every\npixel of direction comes from the guides and the prompt.\n\n**The old batch route (LTXVAddGuidesFromBatch + a padded guide video) is gone:** its transport required the\nguide clip to carry \"no pin\" as **byte-exact black**, and any noisy padding frame became an accidental guide\n(the measured E23 trap). The chain has no padding, so the trap is gone with it.\n\n**Knobs:** the two `LoadImage` stills (pick the key moments), the two **`frame_idx`** widgets (the pin\npositions on the 97-frame timeline), strength 1.0 shared. Canvas 768x768 (multiples of 32), 97 frames\n(8n+1), fps 25 on CreateVideo.\n\n*Measured: the batch route is E23; the chained route is its addendum in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*\n\n*How to run it: story **S36** in HOWTO.md  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E23** in \u000bideo/EXPERIMENTS.md.*\n\n**Measured (E23 addendum):** the chained route reproduces the batch route behavior exactly (A/B on the same stills - mean-color traces match frame-for-frame). And the transition character is **content-driven**: a close-up portrait vs a distant wide scene = LTX resolves it as a shot change (a cut). Keyframe travel reads smoothly when the change is camera/pose level between recognizably-same content (E23 arms B/D/E); shot-change pairs cut, legitimately."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## ltxv-guides.json\n\nKeyframe animation: our stills pinned at chosen frames\n\n**Does:** two stills + a prompt -> a clip that travels between the stills. **Chained `LTXVAddGuide` route\n(2026-11-23):** each guide node pins one still at its `frame_idx` on the 97-frame timeline - the indices are\n**editable widgets**, no offline guide-clip build. The latent stays empty (`EmptyLTXVLatentVideo`): every\npixel of direction comes from the guides and the prompt.\n\n**The old batch route (LTXVAddGuidesFromBatch + a padded guide video) is gone:** its transport required the\nguide clip to carry \"no pin\" as **byte-exact black**, and any noisy padding frame became an accidental guide\n(the measured E23 trap). The chain has no padding, so the trap is gone with it.\n\n**Knobs:** the two `LoadImage` stills (pick the key moments), the two **`frame_idx`** widgets (the pin\npositions on the 97-frame timeline), strength 1.0 shared. Canvas 768x768 (multiples of 32), 97 frames\n(8n+1), fps 25 on CreateVideo.\n\n*Measured: the batch route is E23; the chained route is its addendum in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*\n\n*How to run it: story **S36** in HOWTO.md  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E23** in \u000bideo/EXPERIMENTS.md.*"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
